  "notes": "USAGE:\nAlso written as {取|と}り{替|か}える. Both kanji spellings ({換|か}える and {替|か}える) are used, with {換|か} emphasizing technical replacement and {替|か} emphasizing general swapping. In practice they are often interchangeable.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {電球|でんきゅう}を{取|と}り{換|か}える: replace a light bulb\n- フィルターを{取|と}り{換|か}える: replace a filter\n- {部品|ぶひん}を{取|と}り{換|か}える: replace a part\n- {新品|しんぴん}に{取|と}り{換|か}える: replace with a new one\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{取|と}り{換|か}える focuses on removing one item and inserting another. {交換|こうかん}する is more formal and often implies a mutual exchange. {入|い}れ{替|か}える emphasizes putting something new in place of the old.",
